# Edera zone kernel variant: IO-throughput guest (token).
#
# There is essentially no build-time IO-throughput lever in a virtio guest: the host
# arbitrates real disk I/O and the guest's block scheduler is a runtime sysfs knob
# (/sys/block/*/queue/scheduler), where 'none' is best and BFQ is actively wrong. So this
# flavor only removes BFQ (it should never be selected in a guest; dropping it also shrinks
# the image and prevents mis-selection). Real IO tuning stays a runtime choice -- run-fio.sh
# compares none/mq-deadline/bfq at runtime to show the kernel image is not the lever.
# CONFIG_IOSCHED_BFQ is not set
